libcoraza (1.8.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 1.8.1.
  * Build against coraza v3.8.1 (was v3.7.0). With CRS, coraza v3.7.0 keeps
    ~170 MB per transaction alive between phases on a 230 KB JSON body, so a
    slow upstream holding many requests open could run nginx workers out of
    memory (coraza-nginx#173); v3.8.1 keeps ~45 MB.

 -- Pierre Pomes <pierre.pomes@gmail.com>  Sat, 14 Nov 2026 13:53:35 -0500

libcoraza (1.8.0-1) unstable; urgency=low

  * New upstream release 1.8.0.
  * Export coraza_is_response_body_accessible(): the response-side counterpart
    of coraza_is_request_body_accessible(). coraza_is_response_body_processable()
    only checks the Content-Type against SecResponseBodyMimeType, so under
    "SecResponseBodyAccess Off" connectors could not tell the body would not
    be inspected and delayed response headers for nothing (coraza-nginx#140,
    coraza-apache#60).
  * Build-Depends: golang-go (>= 2:1.26~), matching the go 1.26.0 directive
    in go.mod (builds on jammy/noble pull it from ppa:longsleep/golang-backports).

 -- Pierre Pomes <pierre.pomes@gmail.com>  Wed, 23 Sep 2026 13:24:44 -0400

